        {
          "title": "Bytecode, JIT and Class Loading",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bytecode and the JIT",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Bytecode== = stack-based, platform-neutral instructions in `.class` files",
                "Engine ==interprets== first, then JIT-compiles **hot** methods to native code",
                "{blue:C1} = quick compile, {purple:C2} = optimizing; ==tiered== uses both"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "javac Hello.java",
                "javap -c Hello"
              ],
              "note": "javap -c disassembles to bytecode"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "JIT tricks: ==inlining==, ==escape analysis==, dead-code elimination",
                "Warm-up cost makes short benchmarks lie: use ==JMH=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Class Loading",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bootstrap",
                    "sub": "core JDK classes",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Platform",
                    "sub": "formerly Extension",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Application",
                    "sub": "classpath",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each loader asks its ==parent first==: user code cannot replace `java.lang.String`",
                "Loading is ==lazy==: on first use",
                "Steps: load → link (verify, prepare, resolve) → ==initialize== (static blocks run)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Missing Class Errors",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ClassNotFoundException",
                "NoClassDefFoundError"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Kind",
                  "**checked** exception",
                  "**Error**"
                ],
                [
                  "When",
                  "dynamic load fails, e.g. `Class.forName`",
                  "present at compile time, missing at runtime"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Delegation goes ==up== to Bootstrap first; a JIT benchmark needs ==warm-up== before timing."
