    {
      "title": "Garbage Collection Basics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Garbage Collection Basics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Is Garbage",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Eligible when no live ==GC root== can reach it",
                "Roots: **thread stacks**, **static fields**, JNI refs",
                "No reference counting, so ==cycles are collected=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Generations and Collectors",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Eden",
                    "sub": "new objects",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "S0 / S1",
                    "sub": "survivors age",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Old",
                    "sub": "promoted at threshold",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Most objects ==die young==",
                "{green:Minor GC}: cleans Young, frequent, fast",
                "{red:Major/Full GC}: Old and more, slow, long ==stop-the-world== pauses"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Collector",
                "Pick it for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Serial",
                  "small apps"
                ],
                [
                  "Parallel",
                  "throughput"
                ],
                [
                  "==G1==",
                  "default since Java 9, balanced low pause"
                ],
                [
                  "ZGC / Shenandoah",
                  "very low pause, large heaps"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Avoid and Tune",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`System.gc()` is only a ==hint==, no guarantee",
                "`finalize()` is deprecated: use try-with-resources or `Cleaner`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "java -Xms512m -Xmx2g \\",
                "     -XX:+UseG1GC -Xlog:gc App"
              ],
              "note": "heap size, collector, GC log"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "GC frees only ==unreachable== objects. Reachable but unused objects are a **leak**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "String Pool and Immutability",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "String Pool and Immutability",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Immutable and Pooled",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Immutable==: value fixed after creation",
                "`concat`, `replace`, `toUpperCase` return a **new** String",
                "==String pool==: unique literals cached in the heap (Java 7+)",
                "Same literal text shares **one** object"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`\"hi\"`",
                  "reuses or creates the pooled one"
                ],
                [
                  "`new String(\"hi\")`",
                  "always a new heap object"
                ],
                [
                  "`s.intern()`",
                  "returns the pooled instance"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`==` compares references; `equals()` compares content"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "String b = new String(\"a\");",
                "System.out.println(\"a\" == \"a\");",
                "System.out.println(b == \"a\");",
                "System.out.println(b.equals(\"a\"));"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "true",
                "false",
                "true"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why Immutable, and Loops",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Safe pool sharing",
                "Thread safety",
                "Cached `hashCode`: safe HashMap keys",
                "Security: class names, paths, credentials"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Concat in loop",
                "Thread-safe",
                "Speed"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`s +=`",
                  "n/a",
                  "many garbage objects"
                ],
                [
                  "`StringBuilder`",
                  "no",
                  "fast"
                ],
                [
                  "`StringBuffer`",
                  "synchronized",
                  "slower"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Compare content with ==equals()==, never `==`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Memory Leaks and Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Memory Leaks and Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Leak Is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Leak = objects still ==reachable== but never used again",
                "GC cannot free them, so it ends in `OutOfMemoryError`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cause",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Static collection only grows",
                  "Bounded cache or `WeakHashMap`"
                ],
                [
                  "Unclosed stream, connection",
                  "try-with-resources"
                ],
                [
                  "Listener never deregistered",
                  "Remove listener on close"
                ],
                [
                  "ThreadLocal in thread pool",
                  "`remove()` in `finally`"
                ],
                [
                  "Bad equals/hashCode key",
                  "Override both consistently"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Diagnose",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Find the pid, check the heap, dump live objects",
                "Open `heap.hprof` in ==Eclipse MAT== or VisualVM",
                "Add `-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError` to the JVM flags"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "jps",
                "jcmd <pid> GC.heap_info",
                "jmap -dump:live,format=b,file=heap.hprof <pid>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cheat Sheet",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==JDK ⊃ JRE ⊃ JVM==",
                "`javac` then `java`; `javap -c` shows bytecode",
                "Class loaders delegate to the parent first",
                "Stack **per thread**, heap **shared**",
                "Young → Old generations, ==G1== default",
                "`equals()` for content, never `==`",
                "`StringBuilder` in loops",
                "Heap dump on OOM"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pooled threads live on",
              "text": "A pooled thread never dies, so its ==ThreadLocal== values stay. Always `remove()` in `finally`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What do `\"hi\" == new String(\"hi\")` and `\"hi\".equals(new String(\"hi\"))` print?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`false`, then `true`",
                "`new String` always makes a fresh heap object; the literal is the pooled one",
                "`==` compares references, `equals()` compares content"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A service adds every request to a static List and never removes anything. It ends in OutOfMemoryError. Will a bigger -Xmx fix it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No, it only delays the crash",
                "The static field is a GC root, so the objects stay reachable and GC cannot free them",
                "Fix: bound the cache or remove entries"
              ]
            },
            {
              "query": "",
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Class.forName(\"Missing\") fails at runtime. Which is thrown, and is it checked?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "ClassNotFoundException, which is checked",
                "NoClassDefFoundError is the unchecked Error: the class was there at compile time but is missing at runtime"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
